-- query result cache: year(<date>) is non-deterministic (not cached), unlike toYear(<date>)
-- toYear(<date>) is deterministic and caches
1
-- year(<date>) is rejected from the query cache
-- niladic year() is rejected from the query cache too
-- only the deterministic toYear(<date>) query is cached
1
-- Replicated mutations: year(<date>) is rejected (non-deterministic), toYear(<date>) is accepted
-- the toYear(<date>) DELETE mutation was accepted and completed
(DELETE WHERE toYear(ts) = 2024)	1
-- year(<date>) mutation is rejected as non-deterministic
-- index analysis: year(<date>) still prunes granules like toYear(<date>) (post-build analysis is unaffected by determinism)
-- year(d) prunes to the same granule fraction as toYear(d), and prunes at all
1
1
-- projections: year(<date>) filters/keys still select projections like toYear(<date>)
-- normal projection is chosen for both toYear(ts) and year(ts) filters
1
1
-- force_optimize_projection = 1 succeeds for year(ts) (would throw PROJECTION_NOT_USED if rejected), same result as toYear(ts)
730
730
-- aggregate projection is chosen for a year(ts) GROUP BY, and force_optimize_projection = 1 succeeds
1
